# scan() of Bun.Glob is written in JavaScript. No operation names Bun.Glob here: Link follows Bun to it and is told of the construction, which lays scan() above what it makes. The program does not hold its function: a call would find nothing to run.
# A function of the host's library is listed as one of the engine's is. What only the product of native code and the names of protocols brings is not: a build does not stop for it.
# new Bun.Glob("*.js").scan(".");
# LIBRARY: own
# RUN(FOUND): link lookups mechanisms=all
# FOUND: lookup called BunGlob
# FOUND: lookup native-code-may-hold-objects
# RUN: lacked
# CHECK: lacked GlobScan
# RUN(PRODUCT): lacked
# PRODUCT-NOT: lacked JSIteratorPrototypeDispose

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
function f0 module=m0 kind=Module thisType={type=anything} results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = Builtin builtin=Bun
    v1 = PropGet v0 key="Glob"
    v2 = String string="*.js"
    v3 = Construct v1, -, v2 calleeName="Bun.Glob"
    v4 = PropGet v3 key="scan"
    v5 = String string="."
    v6 = Call v4, v3, v5 calleeKey="scan"
    v7 = Undefined
    Return v7
}
